  "_comment": "Rooms behind locked doors (docs/02-game-design.md \"Puertas con llave\"), drawn on floor 7 from (0,0). Read by doors.test.ts here and by server/internal/session (TestDoorRoomsFixture), so make validate and the server agree on every room and on every locked door they refuse. Tiles: . grass; T grass and the island temple (the world of the escape check; without a T the temple is the first tile of . T d P K, row by row, as server worldtest draws it); # wall; D locked door, closed; d locked door, placed open; K locked door of another key, closed; P plain door, closed; X plain door on a tile that a wall blocks too; space: no tile. {\"repeat\": n, \"row\": r} stands for n rows r, and {\"repeat\": n, \"rows\": [r1, r2, ...]} for those rows n times. portals: teleports on floor 7 by \"x,y\" (an edge of the escape check from the area of from to the area of to). houses: houses by \"x,y,w,h\" (their rect on floor 7), with a door and an exit by \"x,y\": their tiles are walls of the areas, and a player stands in them (an owner or a guest). rooms: tiles behind each locked door by \"x,y\"; error: why the first refused locked door is refused, and door: that door by \"x,y\" (for bypass, the first door of the room a player gets into without its key). First each door in map order (chunk by chunk, row by row): walled (no side), open (one side), truncated (two sides or more bigger than 4096 tiles), tie (the two biggest sides have the same size) or key (it shares its room with a locked door of another key). Then, with every room worked out, the escape check: escape (a side of a door reaches no temple without keys, on foot, out of rooms through their doors and by portals: a vault no door guards) and then bypass (a player with every key but the door's, anywhere outside the rooms or in a house, gets into its room: a locked door of another key opens onto it from its own room).",
